{"page_content": "ACME/Flame Design Final Report (2023) \n \n6 April 2023 \n109 \n \n \n\u2022 \nScience in St. Louis Seminar Series: Fire in Space (8 March 2018) \n\u2022 \nInternational Space Station (ISS) Combustion Experiments (15 Oct. 2018) \n\u2022 \nInternational Space Station experiments will search for key to soot-free flames (14 May 2019) \n\u2022 \nLighting A Flame In Space Could Help Fuels Burn More Cleanly On Earth (21 May 2019) \n\u2022 \nDon\u2019t Light a Fire on the International Space Station\u2026Unless it\u2019s for Science (at 1:03:06, 8 Jan. \n2020) \n\u2022 \nIn space, flames become otherworldly (30 Aug. 2022) - while general to ACME, the photo \ncollage was from 2019 normal-flame testing for Flame Design.  Despite its one-paragraph \nbrevity, Sunderland and Stocker were both interviewed for this article which was published \nunder the title Cosmic Combustion on page 22 of the Oct. 2022 issue of the National \nGeographic Magazine. \n \nStocker is involved in a broad range of NASA educational outreach to students and teachers, Scouts \nof both genders, and the general public.  His primary outreach focus is the fundamentals of \nmicrogravity and human spaceflight, for example through microgravity design challenges which he \nhelps create and administer. But he periodically addresses other topics, e.g., where he sometimes \nspeaks on \u2018NASA and the Science of Superman\u2019 \u2013 for example at the Superman Celebration in \nMetropolis, IL.  In this regard, his NASA outreach is carried out locally, regionally, nationally, and \nonline.  For example, he regularly presents on microgravity at Space Center Houston\u2019s Space \nExploration Educators Conference (SEEC).   He has exhibited the last five National Scout Jamborees, \nfive national Boy Scout conferences, the last three national Girl Scout conventions, and the 2019 \nWorld Scout Jamboree (which was held in the U.S.).  Stocker has been a key lead for the agency in \nNASA\u2019s participation in these Scouting events, where as an example the latter outreach is visually \ndescribed at www.nasa.gov/feature/stem/world-scout-jamboree.html.", "metadata": {"source": "PSI-10_Reports_FinalRpt_ACMEFlameDesign.pdf", "page": 109}}